# Campaign Math

Treat campaign calculations as business-critical logic. Use the `campaign-calculation-change` skill for any formula change.

## Purity and determinism

Pure TypeScript. No side effects, no I/O, no `Date.now()`, no `Math.random()`, no randomness. Same inputs must always produce same outputs.

Never add a model, heuristic, scoring function, or AI call. Status is rule precedence over named alerts, not a composite score.

## Never silently change

- turnout assumptions
- win-number formulas
- voter propensity definitions
- voter universe definitions
- support assumptions
- persuasion assumptions
- contact-rate assumptions
- GOTV assumptions

Before changing campaign math:

1. identify the existing formula
2. identify the assumptions
3. identify downstream calculations
4. provide a worked numerical example
5. add regression tests

## Registries and versioning

`metricRegistry.ts` and `assumptionRegistry.ts` hold stable keys. Never use bare string keys at call sites.

Formula IDs carry a version suffix (`victory.vote_goal.v0.2`). Behavior changes require a new formula ID and `MATH_ENGINE_VERSION` bump in `index.ts`.

`calibration.ts` defines profile SHAPE only — no empirical values. Real estimates live in private `@wings/calibration-profiles`.

NEVER hard-code a strategic cushion. Target share defaults to the mathematical 50% baseline.

## Universe and capacity

Strategic Desired, Reachable, and Capacity-Supported universes are distinct stages. Reachability gap and capacity gap are reported separately.

Shared resource pools with explicit channel allocations. Two channels sharing a pool MUST NOT each see the full pool. See `docs/PROGRAM_BUDGET_CAPACITY_MODEL.md` before touching `programBudget.ts` or `capacity.ts`.

## Tests

Tests are `.cjs` files under `tests/`. Every new formula gets a unit test. Fixtures use invented round numbers, never plausible real-world ones. Test normal, zero, boundary, and missing values.

Keep shared calculations centralized. Do not duplicate campaign math across components.
